-- 041: Deep content + matching exercises for X05 · Data Analysis with EDA.
UPDATE public.sessions SET
 content_en = E'## Why EDA comes before conclusions\n\n**Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)** is the detective phase: before you claim anything, you look at the data from every angle — shape, spread, gaps, relationships. Skipping it is how analysts ship confident, wrong conclusions. We keep exploring TokoSegar''s sales.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Univariate analysis — one variable at a time\n\nLook at each variable alone first:\n\n| Question | Tool | Reveals |\n|----------|------|---------|\n| What is typical? | mean, median | central tendency |\n| How spread out? | std dev, range, IQR | variability |\n| What is the shape? | histogram | skew, peaks |\n| Any extremes? | box plot | outliers |\n\n> A histogram of basket size that leans right (a long high-value tail) tells you the mean will overstate the "typical" basket — reach for the median.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Bivariate analysis — two variables together\n\n| Pair of variables | Tool | Reveals |\n|-------------------|------|---------|\n| number vs number | scatter plot, correlation | does one move with the other? |\n| category vs number | grouped bar, box-by-group | which group is higher? |\n| category vs category | cross-tab (pivot) | co-occurrence |\n\n**Correlation** runs from −1 to +1: near +1 rise together, near −1 one rises as the other falls, near 0 no linear link. Correlation is **not** causation.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Observation → Insight → Recommendation\n\nThe ladder that turns data into value:\n\n| Level | Example |\n|-------|---------|\n| **Observation** | "Jakarta revenue is 40% of the total." |\n| **Insight** | "Jakarta over-indexes because premium members cluster there and buy Electronics." |\n| **Recommendation** | "Pilot a premium-Electronics bundle in Jakarta next quarter." |\n\nEvery finding should pass the **"so what?"** test — if you cannot answer *so what should we do*, keep digging.\n\n---\n\n## 4. An end-to-end EDA flow\n\n```\nUnderstand the columns → types, meaning, units\n↓\nClean & sanity-check → ranges, missing, duplicates\n↓\nUnivariate → distribution + outliers of each key field\n↓\nBivariate → relationships that answer the question\n↓\nInsight + recommendation → the "so what"\n```\n\n> **Mini case study.** Exploring returns, a scatter of `discount %` vs `return rate` showed a clear upward trend. Observation: deeper discounts, more returns. Insight: heavy discounting attracts one-off deal-seekers who return more. Recommendation: cap discounts on return-prone categories.\n\n---\n\n## Common pitfalls\n\n- **Jumping to bivariate before univariate.** You miss the outlier that distorts every correlation.\n- **Correlation = causation.** A lurking third variable (season, promo) often drives both.\n- **Averaging away the story.** Segments can move in opposite directions the average hides (Simpson''s paradox).\n- **Stopping at the observation.** Numbers without a "so what" are trivia.\n\n---\n\n## Glossary\n\n| Term | Meaning |\n|------|---------|\n| Univariate | Analysis of a single variable |\n| Bivariate | Analysis of two variables together |\n| Distribution | The shape of how values spread |\n| Correlation | Strength/direction of a linear relationship (−1..+1) |\n| Insight | An observation explained — the why behind it |\n\n---\n\n## Key Takeaways\n\n1. EDA is the look-before-you-leap phase — shape, spread, gaps, relationships.\n2. Do **univariate** first (distribution, outliers), then **bivariate** (relationships).\n3. Correlation is direction + strength, **not** cause.\n4. Climb the ladder: **observation → insight → recommendation**, and pass the **"so what?"** test.\n5. Beware averages that hide opposing segment trends.\n\n> 💡 Practice with the matching exercises below, then run an end-to-end EDA on the assignment case.',
 content_id = E'## Kenapa EDA sebelum kesimpulan\n\n**Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)** adalah fase detektif: sebelum mengklaim apa pun, Anda melihat data dari segala sudut — bentuk, sebaran, celah, hubungan. Melewatinya adalah cara analyst menghasilkan kesimpulan yang percaya diri tapi salah. Kita lanjut mengeksplorasi penjualan TokoSegar.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Analisis univariate — satu variabel per waktu\n\nLihat tiap variabel sendirian dulu:\n\n| Pertanyaan | Alat | Mengungkap |\n|------------|------|-----------|\n| Apa yang tipikal? | mean, median | pemusatan |\n| Seberapa menyebar? | std dev, range, IQR | variabilitas |\n| Apa bentuknya? | histogram | kemiringan, puncak |\n| Ada ekstrem? | box plot | outlier |\n\n> Histogram basket size yang miring ke kanan (ekor nilai tinggi yang panjang) memberi tahu bahwa mean akan melebih-lebihkan basket "tipikal" — pakai median.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Analisis bivariate — dua variabel bersama\n\n| Pasangan variabel | Alat | Mengungkap |\n|-------------------|------|-----------|\n| angka vs angka | scatter plot, korelasi | apakah bergerak bersama? |\n| kategori vs angka | grouped bar, box per grup | grup mana lebih tinggi? |\n| kategori vs kategori | cross-tab (pivot) | ko-okurensi |\n\n**Korelasi** berkisar −1 sampai +1: dekat +1 naik bersama, dekat −1 satu naik saat lain turun, dekat 0 tak ada kaitan linear. Korelasi **bukan** sebab-akibat.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Observasi → Insight → Rekomendasi\n\nTangga yang mengubah data jadi nilai:\n\n| Level | Contoh |\n|-------|--------|\n| **Observasi** | "Revenue Jakarta 40% dari total." |\n| **Insight** | "Jakarta over-index karena member premium menumpuk di sana dan beli Electronics." |\n| **Rekomendasi** | "Uji coba bundle premium-Electronics di Jakarta kuartal depan." |\n\nSetiap temuan harus lolos uji **"so what?"** — kalau Anda tak bisa menjawab *jadi apa yang harus dilakukan*, teruslah menggali.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Alur EDA end-to-end\n\n```\nPahami kolom → tipe, makna, satuan\n↓\nBersihkan & cek kewajaran → rentang, hilang, duplikat\n↓\nUnivariate → distribusi + outlier tiap field kunci\n↓\nBivariate → hubungan yang menjawab pertanyaan\n↓\nInsight + rekomendasi → "so what"-nya\n```\n\n> **Studi kasus mini.** Mengeksplorasi retur, scatter `diskon %` vs `return rate` menunjukkan tren naik jelas. Observasi: diskon lebih dalam, retur lebih banyak. Insight: diskon besar menarik pemburu deal sesaat yang lebih sering retur. Rekomendasi: batasi diskon pada kategori rawan retur.\n\n---\n\n## Kesalahan umum\n\n- **Loncat ke bivariate sebelum univariate.** Anda melewatkan outlier yang mendistorsi setiap korelasi.\n- **Korelasi = sebab.** Variabel ketiga tersembunyi (musim, promo) sering menggerakkan keduanya.\n- **Merata-ratakan cerita.** Segmen bisa bergerak berlawanan yang disembunyikan rata-rata (paradoks Simpson).\n- **Berhenti di observasi.** Angka tanpa "so what" hanya trivia.\n\n---\n\n## Glosarium\n\n| Istilah | Arti |\n|---------|------|\n| Univariate | Analisis satu variabel |\n| Bivariate | Analisis dua variabel bersama |\n| Distribusi | Bentuk sebaran nilai |\n| Korelasi | Kekuatan/arah hubungan linear (−1..+1) |\n| Insight | Observasi yang dijelaskan — alasan di baliknya |\n\n---\n\n## Kesimpulan Utama\n\n1. EDA adalah fase lihat-dulu-sebelum-melompat — bentuk, sebaran, celah, hubungan.\n2. Lakukan **univariate** dulu (distribusi, outlier), lalu **bivariate** (hubungan).\n3. Korelasi adalah arah + kekuatan, **bukan** sebab.\n4. Naiki tangga: **observasi → insight → rekomendasi**, dan lolos uji **"so what?"**.\n5. Waspadai rata-rata yang menyembunyikan tren segmen yang berlawanan.\n\n> 💡 Latih dengan exercise matching di bawah, lalu jalankan EDA end-to-end pada case tugas.'
WHERE session_number = 'X05';

INSERT INTO public.exercises (session_id, type, title_en, title_id, description_en, description_id, starter_code, solution_code, test_cases, hints_en, hints_id, difficulty, order_num)
SELECT s.id, 'matching', 'EDA Terms', 'Istilah EDA',
  'Match each EDA term to its meaning.', 'Cocokkan setiap istilah EDA dengan artinya.',
  '{"pairs":[{"left":"Univariate","right":"Analysis of one variable"},{"left":"Bivariate","right":"Analysis of two variables together"},{"left":"Outlier","right":"A value far from the rest"},{"left":"Distribution","right":"The shape of how values spread"}]}','',
  '[{"id":"tc1","validation_type":"matching","expected_value":"Analysis of one variable","description_en":"Univariate","description_id":"Univariate","points":25},{"id":"tc2","validation_type":"matching","expected_value":"Analysis of two variables together","description_en":"Bivariate","description_id":"Bivariate","points":25},{"id":"tc3","validation_type":"matching","expected_value":"A value far from the rest","description_en":"Outlier","description_id":"Outlier","points":25},{"id":"tc4","validation_type":"matching","expected_value":"The shape of how values spread","description_en":"Distribution","description_id":"Distribusi","points":25}]',
  '["Uni = one, bi = two","An outlier stands apart"]','["Uni = satu, bi = dua","Outlier menyendiri"]','easy',1
FROM public.sessions s WHERE s.session_number='X05' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM public.exercises e WHERE e.session_id=s.id AND e.title_en='EDA Terms');

